WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:02.030
- Today's going to be a bit special

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:05.010
because today's video is a reaction video.

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:07.000
We will together look at a video

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.090
from one of the very
large content creator's

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:12.620
in the sphere of consulting out there.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:14.080
Her name is Kchoi.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.630
I trust that many of you
have already come across

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:18.070
of some of her videos.

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:21.410
I believe she does great content
on the topic of consulting.

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:23.500
I inserted a link to the channel below

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:25.540
in the video description so check it out

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:26.470
if you want to see more.

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:28.360
In the video we're going
to talk about today,

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:30.030
she is talking about the pros

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.950
and cons of consulting
from her perspective.

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:34.330
And I believe that consulting

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:36.670
is a very heterogeneous field with lots

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:38.880
of different types of firms present.

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:40.440
So while now I watching the video,

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:43.320
I will frequently stop
and share my experiences

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:45.690
as a former McKinsey consultant.

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:47.930
I will reflect on what she is saying,

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:49.480
and then give you my perspective

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:51.890
on whether I believe
that this is also true

00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:55.360
for an MBB context or where
there might be some differences.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:57.410
So trust, this is really
going to be valuable

00:00:57.410 --> 00:01:00.210
for you if you are asking
yourself whether consulting

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:02.710
is the right career
choice for you to pursue.

00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:04.980
So welcome on my channel Firm Learning,

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:08.260
but now without further
ado, let's jump into it.

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:10.640
- The first pro is that
when you're a consultant,

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:13.470
you usually get to work in a
lot of different industries.

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:16.460
This is great if you don't
have a particular interest

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:18.560
or passion in one industry,

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:20.910
whether that's healthcare
or consumer goods

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:23.160
or anything like that
because in consulting,

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:25.920
you usually get access and opportunities

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:28.510
in all different kinds of industries.

00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:30.550
- So let me start here.

00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:32.960
What she says is that
usually as a consultant

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:35.070
you get access to lots of industries,

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:37.150
and of course, this is true,

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:39.110
and this is correct in general.

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:40.290
Though be mindful here,

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:43.280
which consulting firm
exactly you are joining.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:45.850
And just as in one example in Germany,

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:49.571
there exists the large
consulting firm Roland Berger

00:01:49.571 --> 00:01:51.747
and their structure is
that they are structured

00:01:51.747 --> 00:01:54.200
in different competence centers.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:57.810
And the usual way to
enter to start working

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:00.180
at Roland Berger is
that from the beginning,

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:03.810
you directly to commit to one
of these competence centers.

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:05.390
And then in most cases,

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:07.410
at least this is my understanding.

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:09.810
You will work the majority of your time

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:12.180
for the industry of the competence center

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:13.330
that you're part of.

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:15.820
Understand that there are
also some opportunities

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:18.280
to start as a generalist at Roland Berger,

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:19.820
but this is just one example.

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:21.280
Then there are others as well,

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:23.220
for instance, at Oliver Wyman,

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:26.510
as far as I'm informed, there
is a financial service's arm.

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:28.790
If you join there then
you will be dedicated

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:31.010
to the financial services practice.

00:02:31.010 --> 00:02:33.430
So inform yourself, really make sure

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:35.350
that you understand
what the company really

00:02:35.350 --> 00:02:37.833
is doing, obviously,
before you start there.

00:02:37.833 --> 00:02:40.200
- This is something I
really appreciate about

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:43.190
my job because I always get
to be learning new things.

00:02:43.190 --> 00:02:45.290
Now the flip side or the con to this

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:48.350
is that you can tend
to become a generalist

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:50.110
in lots of different industries

00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:53.240
and not have a particular
expertise in any single one.

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:56.140
Over time, it is possible and normal

00:02:56.140 --> 00:03:00.220
to gain an expertise in a
particular industry or issue,

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:02.160
but that obviously takes some time.

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:03.950
So at least in the beginning...

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.010
- So here, I would say at least based

00:03:06.010 --> 00:03:08.400
on my experience at McKinsey,

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:11.400
I'd say it's kind of right
and wrong at the same time.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:12.650
It's right in the sense that,

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:14.270
of course in the beginning,

00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:16.220
you will not be a super deep expert

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:18.540
in one specific topic
and it takes some time

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:19.620
as she's also saying.

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:22.950
And yes, if you really
switch industry to industry,

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:24.220
then will be quite hard for you

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:27.230
and will take some time
until you really gain

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:29.780
this deep industry expertise.

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:32.060
But the other side of things is that,

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:35.410
especially if you decide
to early on pursue projects

00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:37.990
that are specifically
in one industry only,

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:40.240
or at least the majority of projects

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:42.090
in that specific industry,

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:43.710
I would argue that you

00:03:43.710 --> 00:03:46.910
will build industry expertise much quicker

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:48.660
and much more deeply than you would

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:51.790
in an average corporate
role in the industry.

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:54.380
And the reason is that
you will do projects

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:57.660
in all different types of
companies of that industry,

00:03:57.660 --> 00:04:00.760
seeing lots of different
functions in the industry,

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:05.700
working together with very
senior employees of the industry.

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:09.080
And I trust this is really
the accelerated type

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:11.100
of career development and experience.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:14.310
And if you want to try to get
a similar experience like that

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:16.220
in industry, if you just start in one

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:19.220
of a normal industry
role in that industry,

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:22.120
this will be difficult and it
would take your much longer.

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:23.080
So from that sense,

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:25.780
I would argue that actually in consulting,

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:26.940
you can gain and collect

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:30.150
that industry experience
much more quickly than

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:32.320
if you would just start at
an average corporate role.

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:34.530
- I think part of your career and at least

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:35.970
for the first several years,

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:38.300
you're probably going to be working

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:41.850
in an array of industries
rather than focusing

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:44.610
in on a single one depending
on the firm you're at.

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:46.910
So maybe you're at a consulting firm

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:49.570
that has a very specific
focus, but in general,

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:52.750
as a consultant, you're working
from industry to industry.

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:54.960
So you tend to get a little bit

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:56.580
of a surface level knowledge

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:59.711
across all different
kinds of industries so...

00:04:59.711 --> 00:05:01.160
- And here, I just want to add,

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:03.740
or just kind of sharpen
your perception that

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:07.070
it's really important what
your consulting background is.

00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:10.750
So from what type of consulting
firm you're coming from.

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:13.444
And I think what's important
to understand is that Kchoi,

00:05:13.444 --> 00:05:15.400
as far as I understand her profile,

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:17.810
she is coming from a rather boutique type

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:18.690
of consulting firm.

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:21.220
She's coming from a change
management consulting firm

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:25.600
and firms like that focus
on really one specific topic

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:27.330
in that case change management.

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:30.230
And now, this is accurate
how I see her profile

00:05:30.230 --> 00:05:33.650
and this knowledge is to be
contrasted with firms like MBB

00:05:33.650 --> 00:05:36.090
or even other like large
strategy consulting firms,

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:38.870
also tier two strategy consulting firms

00:05:38.870 --> 00:05:39.756
that have a much broader perspective

00:05:39.756 --> 00:05:42.840
of tasks that they work.

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:44.443
So the types of projects that you will

00:05:44.443 --> 00:05:46.630
do will be much broader,

00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:49.642
which will help you to gain a
much more deep understanding

00:05:49.642 --> 00:05:51.090
of a certain industry.

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:52.430
- Second pro, which is related

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:55.290
is that you get to work on
lots of different projects.

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:57.710
So not only do you get
to work in different

00:05:57.710 --> 00:05:58.880
and with different companies,

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:01.250
but you also get to do different projects

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:03.210
as in solve different issues for them.

00:06:03.210 --> 00:06:04.510
In the video that I mentioned

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:06.040
at the beginning of this video,

00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:08.670
I sort of break down what
those different issues are.

00:06:08.670 --> 00:06:10.810
So you can check that
out, to learn a bit more.

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:13.210
For me, I work on multiple
different projects

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:15.430
for different clients at the same time.

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:17.540
There are other
consultancies where you are

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:21.380
on one project for a set number of months.

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:22.250
- And just to add in here,

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:26.290
now from the MBB perspective
here in the first years,

00:06:26.290 --> 00:06:30.000
you will always like 99% of the times,

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:32.560
you will be dedicated to one project.

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:35.830
You will not work at
different projects separately.

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:40.310
This only starts once you
are a senior project lead,

00:06:40.310 --> 00:06:42.080
once you want to make the transition

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:44.020
to become a junior partner,

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:45.380
this is the menu start,

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:47.720
maybe leading and have been responsible

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:50.260
for two or three projects in parallel.

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:52.440
But this is now a step in the career

00:06:52.440 --> 00:06:54.620
that is many years down the line.

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:57.870
So in the first three,
four, or five years,

00:06:57.870 --> 00:06:59.110
this is not what will happen.

00:06:59.110 --> 00:07:01.420
You will be dedicated to one project

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:03.250
and at least not relative to the types

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:05.510
of projects that you will do at MBB,

00:07:05.510 --> 00:07:08.460
but also time wise be
completely impossible

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:10.450
to different projects or many projects,

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:12.770
as parallel regarding your time budget,

00:07:12.770 --> 00:07:15.030
this just would not be feasible.

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:16.170
- But either way,

00:07:16.170 --> 00:07:17.990
you get to switch out your projects

00:07:17.990 --> 00:07:20.630
and do something a little
new every single time.

00:07:20.630 --> 00:07:22.090
The con is that naturally,

00:07:22.090 --> 00:07:24.530
you're gonna like some
projects more than others.

00:07:24.530 --> 00:07:26.970
So you're gonna have some
ups and downs in terms

00:07:26.970 --> 00:07:28.560
of how much you're enjoying your work.

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:30.700
You might be staffed on a
project for three months

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:32.420
that you absolutely love.

00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:34.330
And then the next one comes along

00:07:34.330 --> 00:07:36.240
and it's a six-month project

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:38.020
that you're just not as passionate about

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:39.513
or excited about as you move.

00:07:40.429 --> 00:07:42.010
- Yes, I can fully agree with that.

00:07:42.010 --> 00:07:43.560
That is completely accurate.

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:46.900
For sure doesn't matter to
what consultant you talk to.

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:48.260
Everybody reconfirm that there

00:07:48.260 --> 00:07:50.400
are some projects that they really liked.

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:51.930
And then there are some projects

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:54.740
that were really bad for
all kinds of reasons, right?

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:56.300
This is completely normal,

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:58.860
but here I'd say the
positive if now I compare

00:07:58.860 --> 00:08:00.560
that to a corporate job.

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:02.550
That it's even more digital, right?

00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:04.520
I mean, either you get
along with your team,

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:06.050
you get along with your boss,

00:08:06.050 --> 00:08:09.770
you like your work or you end
up actually not liking it.

00:08:09.770 --> 00:08:12.640
But what you do in a corporate
role, if you don't like it?

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:14.840
Then pretty much the only choice

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:18.280
that you have is either to
transition within the company,

00:08:18.280 --> 00:08:19.670
if that is even possible,

00:08:19.670 --> 00:08:22.560
or really need to quit your job
and look for something else.

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:24.340
But the positive thing in consulting

00:08:24.340 --> 00:08:26.740
from my perspective at least is that yes,

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:29.260
maybe there was a bad project which went

00:08:29.260 --> 00:08:31.980
on for a couple of months
that you really disliked.

00:08:31.980 --> 00:08:34.180
But then this project will be over.

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:37.417
Then you can now completely
go out there on a new choice.

00:08:37.417 --> 00:08:39.100
You can go on a new project,

00:08:39.100 --> 00:08:41.130
you can work together with new people.

00:08:41.130 --> 00:08:42.210
And then over time,

00:08:42.210 --> 00:08:43.220
you get to know the people

00:08:43.220 --> 00:08:44.877
that you really enjoy working with.

00:08:44.877 --> 00:08:46.580
You better understand for yourself,

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:48.930
what the projects are
that you enjoy doing.

00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:50.380
And then can actively start

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:52.477
to pursuing these types of projects

00:08:52.477 --> 00:08:55.110
and these types of
colleagues, more and more.

00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:57.460
- Move up in your career
and gain more experience

00:08:57.460 --> 00:09:00.400
then you can start to not
only gain more expertise

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:02.750
in a specific area but also have more

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:04.410
of a say in the projects that you're on.

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:05.530
But when you're first starting out

00:09:05.530 --> 00:09:07.130
and in those first several years,

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:08.870
you have to work a little bit harder

00:09:08.870 --> 00:09:11.300
to get the projects that you want to get.

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:12.940
- Also completely agree on that.

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:15.360
So the staffing market, which
she's referring to, right?

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:18.240
So the options of projects that you have,

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:21.810
they very much depend on
your internal reputation.

00:09:21.810 --> 00:09:24.900
So the more you are
considered as a rock star,

00:09:24.900 --> 00:09:26.720
as a high performer,

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:28.820
the more people will
want to work with you.

00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:31.460
So basically, the better choices you have

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:33.510
and now you want to choose your project.

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:36.150
And of course, at the beginning,
nobody really knows you.

00:09:36.150 --> 00:09:38.240
You're kind of one of many new associates

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:40.240
and then you kind of need to earn

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:42.100
and develop your reputation over time.

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:43.410
And this will then take some time

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:46.260
until you have developed
that, but then once you do it,

00:09:46.260 --> 00:09:47.650
it will significantly help you

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:50.190
to then really do only
specifically the projects

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:51.180
that you want to do.

00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:52.610
- Third pro is travel.

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:54.370
Now, not all consultants travel

00:09:54.370 --> 00:09:56.320
because you might have some that are based

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:58.810
in a particular office and all the clients

00:09:58.810 --> 00:10:01.810
are local so there isn't
much traveling going on.

00:10:01.810 --> 00:10:04.000
But a lot of consultants do have to travel

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:06.260
around the US or even internationally

00:10:06.260 --> 00:10:07.300
to meet with their clients.

00:10:07.300 --> 00:10:08.380
Sometimes they'll get staffed

00:10:08.380 --> 00:10:10.750
on a project that is
in a really cool place,

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:13.160
but I would actually say that the pro

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:16.230
from this is not so
much the travel itself,

00:10:16.230 --> 00:10:19.180
but the rewards and
the status that you get

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:21.370
from all that travel. Personally-

00:10:21.370 --> 00:10:22.750
- That is completely accurate.

00:10:22.750 --> 00:10:26.280
So I have a whole wallet
just of bonus cards,

00:10:26.280 --> 00:10:29.110
of all kinds of hotel chains and airlines.

00:10:29.110 --> 00:10:32.620
You know, you have like
all these gold platinum,

00:10:32.620 --> 00:10:35.690
diamond status cards from
all these different chains.

00:10:35.690 --> 00:10:38.330
And then this is something
that you can also leverage

00:10:38.330 --> 00:10:40.940
for your private, for your
personal vacations, right?

00:10:40.940 --> 00:10:43.560
Because then of course it
will be treated accordingly

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:44.890
in these institutions.

00:10:44.890 --> 00:10:47.250
Then you use that for
private reasons as well.

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:50.360
So yes, these are perks
of being a consultant.

00:10:50.360 --> 00:10:51.360
This is correct.

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:53.940
- Most of my projects are based in the US

00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:57.180
and so I've done travel
to Nashville, Houston,

00:10:57.180 --> 00:11:00.170
Philadelphia, kind of all over the US

00:11:00.170 --> 00:11:02.350
and not so much internationally yet.

00:11:02.350 --> 00:11:04.490
I'm definitely always
expressing my interests

00:11:04.490 --> 00:11:07.590
at work and traveling
internationally for a project.

00:11:07.590 --> 00:11:10.400
So hopefully something will
come up that is the right fit.

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:11.970
But usually, when I have a work trip

00:11:11.970 --> 00:11:15.100
and I'm traveling for
client work, I'm just there,

00:11:15.100 --> 00:11:16.850
like the night before a meeting,

00:11:16.850 --> 00:11:18.370
then go to the meeting in the morning

00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:20.490
and then I'm flying
back home that evening.

00:11:20.490 --> 00:11:22.350
So there isn't usually that much time

00:11:22.350 --> 00:11:25.450
to do any actual exploring or traveling.

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:27.990
But because of all the travel that I do,

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:30.620
I gain status with my
preferred airline and hotel.

00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:33.550
So you just get to reap the benefits of...

00:11:33.550 --> 00:11:34.740
- Yeah so here she just said

00:11:34.740 --> 00:11:36.340
that pretty much you'll start

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:37.780
in the morning flying somewhere.

00:11:37.780 --> 00:11:39.250
And then in the evening, she flies out.

00:11:39.250 --> 00:11:41.390
So this is not really the
rhythm that you will have

00:11:41.390 --> 00:11:45.150
on your average MBB project
at a normal MBB project

00:11:45.150 --> 00:11:47.150
and of course, here
there also some changes.

00:11:47.150 --> 00:11:50.230
But usually, you'll fly
in on Monday morning

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:52.550
and then fly out on Thursday evening.

00:11:52.550 --> 00:11:54.820
This is kind your standard workweek.

00:11:54.820 --> 00:11:57.730
And then within the workweek,
like Monday to Thursday,

00:11:57.730 --> 00:12:00.640
you will stay at the work client-side,

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:02.720
and then usually stay at a hotel.

00:12:02.720 --> 00:12:05.490
The only exception of cause
is if you do a project

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:06.760
in your hometown, and then,

00:12:06.760 --> 00:12:08.270
of course, you can just work or stay

00:12:08.270 --> 00:12:09.237
at home then in the evening.

00:12:09.237 --> 00:12:10.350
And then on top of that,

00:12:10.350 --> 00:12:12.330
you might fly out or even other locations,

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:15.210
maybe you have a workshop
within the week in another city,

00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:18.030
in another country, maybe
even in another continent.

00:12:18.030 --> 00:12:19.900
So this is then the travel that even comes

00:12:19.900 --> 00:12:22.040
on top of that, but kind of the baseline

00:12:22.040 --> 00:12:25.280
is staying Monday to
Thursday at your client.

00:12:25.280 --> 00:12:27.020
- Like upgrades and things like that.

00:12:27.020 --> 00:12:29.330
It also means that I can rack up miles

00:12:29.330 --> 00:12:32.940
and be able to make trips
based solely on my miles.

00:12:32.940 --> 00:12:34.986
So I am paying nothing or just paying like

00:12:34.986 --> 00:12:37.140
a $5 fee to book a plane ticket.

00:12:37.140 --> 00:12:39.570
The only con I would say
that comes with traveling

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:41.450
for work is that it is much harder

00:12:41.450 --> 00:12:43.930
to gain a healthy work-life balance.

00:12:43.930 --> 00:12:46.160
It can be hard to get into a routine.

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:49.320
For example, meal prepping
is pretty impossible

00:12:49.320 --> 00:12:52.290
to do if your schedule
is constantly changing,

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:54.390
or even if you're a consultant who travels

00:12:54.390 --> 00:12:55.990
from Monday to Thursday,

00:12:55.990 --> 00:12:58.430
then you're only home for
a few days out of the week.

00:12:58.430 --> 00:13:01.040
So you tend to do things like going out

00:13:01.040 --> 00:13:03.760
to eat instead of prepping your
meals and things like that.

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:04.593
Also, when you-

00:13:04.593 --> 00:13:06.400
- I just want to stress and underline this

00:13:06.400 --> 00:13:08.260
because here again, I completely agree.

00:13:08.260 --> 00:13:11.410
And the problem is that in
most cases, Monday morning,

00:13:11.410 --> 00:13:13.090
you will need to wake up really early

00:13:13.090 --> 00:13:14.880
to get one of the earlier flights.

00:13:14.880 --> 00:13:16.390
So depending a bit on your location,

00:13:16.390 --> 00:13:17.950
the connection often you will need

00:13:17.950 --> 00:13:20.820
to wake up at 5:00 a.m.
sometimes even earlier.

00:13:20.820 --> 00:13:23.960
So this means you'll
ready start your work week

00:13:23.960 --> 00:13:25.780
with some kind of sleep deficit.

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:28.770
And then this just continuous
building over the workweek,

00:13:28.770 --> 00:13:31.080
and then usually on Thursday evening,

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:32.760
or then when the week is over,

00:13:32.760 --> 00:13:35.760
you really need to do lots
of sleeping on the weekend

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:37.100
to recover of course now,

00:13:37.100 --> 00:13:39.760
but depending on your
individual sleep needs.

00:13:39.760 --> 00:13:42.050
But this then leads to really don't having

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:44.250
that much time also not on the weekends.

00:13:44.250 --> 00:13:46.740
And this is of course why this travel can

00:13:46.740 --> 00:13:48.280
be quite a broad and then it adds

00:13:48.280 --> 00:13:51.600
to the not so ideal work-life
balance for many projects.

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:53.170
- You travel a lot for work,

00:13:53.170 --> 00:13:55.400
your work time and personal time tend

00:13:55.400 --> 00:13:56.840
to blend together a lot.

00:13:56.840 --> 00:13:59.290
For example, sometimes
I need to book a flight

00:13:59.290 --> 00:14:01.930
that doesn't get me home
until 11:30 at night,

00:14:01.930 --> 00:14:03.780
which means a lot of my personal time

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:05.220
has been taken up by work.

00:14:05.220 --> 00:14:06.990
Pro no number four is that you get to work

00:14:06.990 --> 00:14:08.620
with a lot of big companies,

00:14:08.620 --> 00:14:11.790
often fortune 100 companies
that are really cool

00:14:11.790 --> 00:14:12.623
and well known.

00:14:12.623 --> 00:14:13.456
That means you might get to go

00:14:13.456 --> 00:14:15.880
to the headquarters of a
really well-known company,

00:14:15.880 --> 00:14:17.550
meet with leaders there.

00:14:17.550 --> 00:14:19.360
And it's just really cool that you get

00:14:19.360 --> 00:14:20.970
to help shape companies

00:14:20.970 --> 00:14:23.083
that are so well known across the world.

00:14:24.275 --> 00:14:25.108
- I agree with that.

00:14:25.108 --> 00:14:27.460
This is indeed what
you will frequently do.

00:14:27.460 --> 00:14:29.540
And of course, it also
depends a bit on your taste.

00:14:29.540 --> 00:14:30.950
So for me personally,

00:14:30.950 --> 00:14:32.650
one of the best experiences I had

00:14:32.650 --> 00:14:33.580
was rather working

00:14:33.580 --> 00:14:36.990
for some more medium-sized
companies in consulting.

00:14:36.990 --> 00:14:38.910
Not necessarily the very big corporates

00:14:38.910 --> 00:14:40.630
and the main reason being that there

00:14:40.630 --> 00:14:43.690
are sometimes at least I
felt like the possibilities

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:44.650
that you have, the things

00:14:44.650 --> 00:14:46.820
that you can really change the time

00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:49.700
to impact the path to
impact was even short.

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:51.270
I was even more direct,

00:14:51.270 --> 00:14:52.250
but now this might also

00:14:52.250 --> 00:14:54.760
be a question of personal preference.

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:56.150
So yes, of course, you really work

00:14:56.150 --> 00:14:57.920
with very large clients

00:14:57.920 --> 00:15:00.530
and you will meet lots of
senior executives this way.

00:15:00.530 --> 00:15:01.980
- Con is that those companies

00:15:01.980 --> 00:15:03.960
and clients could be a lot more demanding.

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:05.410
This is really a generalization

00:15:05.410 --> 00:15:07.990
because some people and
clients you'll just get

00:15:07.990 --> 00:15:10.280
along with better on a personal level,

00:15:10.280 --> 00:15:11.770
just because your working styles

00:15:11.770 --> 00:15:13.140
or your personalities match.

00:15:13.140 --> 00:15:14.530
So regardless of the company,

00:15:14.530 --> 00:15:16.020
there are gonna be some clients

00:15:16.020 --> 00:15:19.020
that are more demanding or
more difficult to work with,

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:21.300
and others that are a
little easier to work with.

00:15:21.300 --> 00:15:23.500
But I would say that the bigger the client

00:15:23.500 --> 00:15:24.910
or more well known the client

00:15:24.910 --> 00:15:26.870
is there's just that much more pressure

00:15:26.870 --> 00:15:30.670
to make sure you're performing
and bringing results, and-

00:15:30.670 --> 00:15:32.470
- So, here I'd say I didn't see

00:15:32.470 --> 00:15:34.190
that correlation that strongly, right?

00:15:34.190 --> 00:15:35.643
I had great clients to work

00:15:35.643 --> 00:15:37.360
with at very large companies

00:15:37.360 --> 00:15:40.070
that are super difficult people to work

00:15:40.070 --> 00:15:42.170
with at smaller companies.

00:15:42.170 --> 00:15:45.860
But overall, I agree that
the type of clients you have,

00:15:45.860 --> 00:15:46.780
or you can work together

00:15:46.780 --> 00:15:49.070
with them really shapes your experience.

00:15:49.070 --> 00:15:51.590
And it can be really hard as a consultant

00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:53.700
if you just don't get along
way with your clients.

00:15:53.700 --> 00:15:55.930
So this is for sure, very decisive factor.

00:15:55.930 --> 00:15:58.400
- Pro number five is that the compensation

00:15:58.400 --> 00:16:00.270
or the pay is usually pretty good.

00:16:00.270 --> 00:16:02.630
According to Glassdoor, the average salary

00:16:02.630 --> 00:16:06.880
for a consultant in the
US is about $79,000,

00:16:06.880 --> 00:16:10.350
which when you compare to a
salary for a software engineer,

00:16:10.350 --> 00:16:12.830
for example, is actually kind of low.

00:16:12.830 --> 00:16:14.700
But when you look at the median salary

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:18.250
in the US as a whole, which is $61,000,

00:16:18.250 --> 00:16:21.080
then it's actually on the
more highly compensated side.

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:23.450
The con is that while
you might earn more money

00:16:23.450 --> 00:16:25.670
than you would in some other careers,

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:28.820
because of some of the
challenges I mentioned earlier

00:16:28.820 --> 00:16:31.290
in the video, like
demanding work schedules

00:16:31.290 --> 00:16:32.930
and difficulty to achieve work,

00:16:32.930 --> 00:16:35.230
life balance, a lot of consultants tend

00:16:35.230 --> 00:16:37.730
to get burned out and leave
after just a few years.

00:16:37.730 --> 00:16:38.860
For example-

00:16:38.860 --> 00:16:40.230
- So here just to react to that.

00:16:40.230 --> 00:16:42.450
So on the salary side,
of course, she is right.

00:16:42.450 --> 00:16:44.100
Yes, consulting, in general,

00:16:44.100 --> 00:16:47.490
is good and rather high paying
career for many of them.

00:16:47.490 --> 00:16:48.870
And then it's also no secret

00:16:48.870 --> 00:16:51.420
that the MBB consulting firms are one

00:16:51.420 --> 00:16:53.560
of the firms that pay the
highest salaries, right?

00:16:53.560 --> 00:16:55.020
So you can expect yourself being

00:16:55.020 --> 00:16:58.000
even at the higher end
of all the spectrum.

00:16:58.000 --> 00:17:00.260
So yes, of course, the salaries are high,

00:17:00.260 --> 00:17:02.620
but what she also rightfully explains

00:17:02.620 --> 00:17:04.200
is that the demands are
high on you as well.

00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:07.470
So you will have a less work-life balance.

00:17:07.470 --> 00:17:09.830
There will be quite a
significant amount of stress

00:17:09.830 --> 00:17:11.180
and pressure on you.

00:17:11.180 --> 00:17:14.200
And yes, some people do
burn out and do struggle.

00:17:14.200 --> 00:17:16.550
And it is also correct
that after some years,

00:17:16.550 --> 00:17:18.730
many leave the consulting firm, though,

00:17:18.730 --> 00:17:20.640
I would argue that this is not only due

00:17:20.640 --> 00:17:23.270
to burnout in the work-life pressure,

00:17:23.270 --> 00:17:26.280
but also just for other
career-related choices as well.

00:17:26.280 --> 00:17:29.580
- Though at BCG, 43% of the employees

00:17:29.580 --> 00:17:31.820
have been there for less than two years

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:34.980
and 77% have been there
for less than five years.

00:17:34.980 --> 00:17:37.270
So despite the pay
because of the lifestyle

00:17:37.270 --> 00:17:39.170
of consulting, a lot of consultants

00:17:39.170 --> 00:17:41.040
tend to leave after just a few years.

00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:43.130
Now as the last pro and flip side

00:17:43.130 --> 00:17:45.260
to that many of these consultants leave

00:17:45.260 --> 00:17:48.500
their jobs because they have
an even better opportunity,

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:50.570
whether it's job at a different company,

00:17:50.570 --> 00:17:52.300
or maybe it's an acceptance

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:53.810
to a prestigious business school.

00:17:53.810 --> 00:17:56.360
Whatever the reason having
that consulting experience

00:17:56.360 --> 00:17:59.300
on your resume makes you
a very valuable asset,

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:01.130
which is why so many people decide

00:18:01.130 --> 00:18:04.240
to go into consulting in the first place.

00:18:04.240 --> 00:18:05.410
- So, yes, I agree with that.

00:18:05.410 --> 00:18:07.720
Consulting is a great career choice

00:18:07.720 --> 00:18:10.070
and also does open many doors for you.

00:18:10.070 --> 00:18:12.350
And especially now with an MBB background,

00:18:12.350 --> 00:18:13.390
these are of course kind

00:18:13.390 --> 00:18:15.360
of household name consulting brands.

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:17.220
And there are different firms

00:18:17.220 --> 00:18:19.990
that really specifically
look out for these profiles

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:20.980
to then hire.

00:18:20.980 --> 00:18:23.100
So yes, if you have this background,

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:24.420
it is a great career choice.

00:18:24.420 --> 00:18:26.090
It can open many doors for you.

00:18:26.090 --> 00:18:27.560
Of course, there are other choices,

00:18:27.560 --> 00:18:29.410
other paths that you can go

00:18:29.410 --> 00:18:32.090
that might provide you with
great opportunities as well.

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:34.250
But of course and this
is from my experience,

00:18:34.250 --> 00:18:38.150
what I've seen, this is
something that might be a path,

00:18:38.150 --> 00:18:39.460
